{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_runtime_overview_runtime_detection", "label": "Runtime-detection model", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/runtime/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A module-load-time check for Bun, then Deno, then process picks the backend, so there is no runtime flag to set: the framework just works on whichever runtime starts it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_runtime_overview_runtime_adapter_layer", "label": "Per-subsystem runtime adapters", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/runtime/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SQLite, TCP, WebSocket server, HTTP server, file I/O and the test runner are the axes that actually differ across runtimes; each has its own adapter file that detects and picks a backend, leaving everything else identical."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_runtime_overview_cross_runtime_cluster", "label": "Cross-runtime cluster", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/runtime/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gossip and transport are wire-format compatible across all three runtimes, which makes mixed runtimes useful for gradual migration; one runtime per cluster is still preferred because stack traces, error messages and perf profiles diverge."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_runtime_overview_runtime_selection_guidance", "label": "Picking a runtime", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/runtime/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bun when you can, Node when the platform requires it, Deno when already invested."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_do